# - Introduces TACE: 'Here we introduce the Tensor Atomic Cluster Expansion (TACE)', constructing 'a controlled many-body hierarchy with atomic cluster expansion (ACE)'; 'Overall, TACE follows the design framework of ACE' (Abstract, Sec. 2.3). Recorded in the registry as TACE derived from ACE. TACE is the method used by the universal model of xu2025 (TACE-v1).
# - The corpus manifest gives the first author as 'Zhixing Xu'; the PDF and the DOI metadata give Zemin Xu, Wenbo Xie and P. Hu. The spec's source block was corrected to Zemin Xu.
# - Table 5's MAE on electric enthalpy is encoded as an energy error (meV/atom); stress (meV/A^3), polarisation, polarisability and Born effective charges are not encoded. Allegro-pol models trained by the authors are not a registry method and are not encoded.
# - Whether the 32-water, GAP17, BaTiO3 and charged-system errors are on test or validation splits is not stated in the tables; no role is recorded. Training settings are in the Methods and SI, which were not encoded beyond channel counts, Lmax and correlation order given with the tables.
# - The 3BPA column headers are reconstructed from the table note (sph/cart, spa/spe, correlation order 2 or 3).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/xu2025spectral.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

